Task #973 — Alert operators when merge-conflict spikes hit a threshold

Adds a scheduled threshold-based alert pipeline on top of the existing
14-day merge-conflict recovery projection so operators are paged when
something regresses in the dev-builder loop, instead of having to watch
the dashboard.

Implementation
- src/repositories/merge-conflict-recovery.repository.ts: new pure
  evaluator `evaluateMergeConflictRecoveryAlerts(summary, thresholds)`
  plus types (`MergeConflictRecoveryAlert`,
  `MergeConflictRecoveryAlertThresholds`) and
  `DEFAULT_MERGE_CONFLICT_RECOVERY_ALERT_THRESHOLDS`. Three independent
  alert families: daily_spike (worst day at/above threshold),
  total_spike (14-day total at/above threshold), and file_dominance
  (a single path crosses BOTH an absolute event-count floor AND a
  ratio-of-total floor). Setting any threshold to 0 disables that
  family.
- src/__tests__/lc4-merge-conflict-recovery-alerts.test.ts: 9 vitest
  cases covering the quiet path, the worst-day-only invariant, ratio
  vs. count interaction for file dominance, all-three-fire, custom
  ratios, and the 0-disables-family contract.
- supabase/functions/merge-conflict-recovery-alerts-cron/index.ts: new
  Deno edge function. Internal-secret auth (mirrors
  command-monitoring-cron). Reads thresholds from env
  (MERGE_CONFLICT_ALERT_DAILY/TOTAL/FILE_COUNT/FILE_RATIO_THRESHOLD),
  fetches events directly from `system.execution_tasks`, projects
  inline, evaluates, and POSTs each alert to the existing
  `alert-dispatcher` (which already handles throttling, flood
  suppression, channel fan-out, and logging).
- supabase/functions/_manifest.ts + supabase/config.toml: register the
  new cron with `verify_jwt = false` and service-role auth class.
- supabase/migrations/20260418200000_merge_conflict_recovery_alerts_cron.sql:
  pg_cron schedule (hourly) using a custom monitored dispatcher
  because the generic `monitored_http_dispatch` only supports Bearer
  auth, while this function uses `x-internal-secret`. Failures land in
  cron_execution_log + DLQ alongside every other cron job.

Notes / deviations
- The pure projection logic in the edge function is duplicated from
  the repository's `projectMergeConflictRecoverySummary` rather than
  shared, because the repository file targets the browser/Vitest
  runtime and the edge function targets Deno. The duplicated logic is
  trivial and the source-of-truth pure function is exhaustively tested
  in vitest.
- All 25 merge-conflict tests (16 projection + 9 alerts) pass locally.
